---
<GenericPage title={page.title} hreflang={hreflang} description={page.description} canonical={page.canonical} ogImage="" bodyHtml={`<header class="entry-header page-title title-align-inherit title-tablet-align-inherit title-mobile-align-inherit"><h1 class="entry-title">Privacy Policy</h1><nav aria-label="Breadcrumbs" class="kadence-breadcrumbs" id="kadence-breadcrumbs"><div class="kadence-breadcrumb-container"><span><a class="kadence-bc-home" href="/" itemprop="url"><span>Home</span></a></span> <span class="bc-delimiter">/</span> <span class="kadence-bread-current">Privacy Policy</span></div></nav></header><div class="entry-content single-content"><p><strong>Effective Date: September 22, 2025</strong></p><p>Welcome to <strong>CholineBio</strong> (“we,” “our,” “us”). We are committed to protecting your personal information and ensuring transparency regarding how we collect, use, store, and share data when you visit <strong><a class="decorated-link" href="/" rel="noopener" target="_new">/</a></strong> or engage with our business services.</p><hr/><h1><strong>1. Data Controller</strong></h1><p>This website is operated by:</p><p><strong>Company Name:</strong> Dinweys (Export Sales Company)<br/><strong>Website:</strong> <a class="decorated-link" href="" rel="noopener" target="_new"></a><br/><strong>Email:</strong> <a class="decorated-link cursor-pointer" rel="noopener"><span class="__cf_email__">[email protected]</span></a></p><p>If you are located in the EU/EEA, Dinweys acts as the <strong>data controller</strong> for your personal data.</p><hr/><h1><strong>2. Information We Collect</strong></h1><p>We may collect the following types of information:</p><h3><strong>A. Information You Provide</strong></h3><p>Examples include:</p><ul><li>Name</li><li>Email address</li><li>Phone number</li><li>Company name and job position</li><li>Address</li><li>Business inquiries, RFQs, order-related details</li><li>Login credentials (if you create an account)</li></ul><h3><strong>B. Automatically Collected Data</strong></h3><p>Collected through cookies and analytics tools:</p><ul><li>IP address</li><li>Browser type and operating system</li><li>Device information</li><li>Pages viewed and time spent</li><li>Referring URLs</li><li>General usage and interaction data</li></ul><h3><strong>C. Information from Third Parties</strong></h3><p>We may receive information from:</p><ul><li>B2B marketplaces (e.g., Alibaba, Made-in-China), if you contact us there</li><li>Social media platforms</li><li>Logistics or payment service providers you authorize</li></ul><hr/><h1><strong>3. How We Use Your Information</strong></h1><p>We may use your information for:</p><ul><li>Responding to RFQs, inquiries, and customer service requests</li><li>Processing orders and providing services</li><li>Improving website functionality and user experience</li><li>Sending updates, business information, or marketing communications (where legally permitted)</li><li>Verifying identity and preventing fraud</li><li>Complying with legal obligations</li></ul><p>We always process data based on a lawful basis (e.g., legitimate interest, consent, or contract performance).</p><hr/><h1><strong>4. Sharing Your Information</strong></h1><p>We do <strong>not</strong> sell your personal data. We may share information only in the following cases:</p><ul><li><strong>Service Providers</strong> (hosting providers, IT security, logistics, email service providers, analytics)</li><li><strong>Legal Compliance</strong> (government requests, legal proceedings, regulatory requirements)</li><li><strong>Business Transfers</strong> (merger, acquisition, restructuring)</li></ul><p>All service providers are required to protect your information under contractual agreements.</p><hr/><h1><strong>5. Cookies &amp; Tracking Technologies</strong></h1><p>We use cookies and related technologies to:</p><ul><li>Improve website performance</li><li>Save your browsing preferences</li><li>Analyze traffic and user behaviors</li><li>Support marketing and remarketing campaigns</li></ul><p>You may disable cookies via your browser settings, but some features may not function properly.</p><p>A full <strong>Cookie Policy</strong> can also be added if needed.</p><hr/><h1><strong>6. Data Security</strong></h1><p>We implement reasonable technical and organizational measures, including:</p><ul><li>SSL/HTTPS encryption</li><li>Limited access control to stored data</li><li>Secure hosting and regular system monitoring</li><li>Periodic security assessments</li></ul><p>While we strive to protect your data, no method of internet transmission is 100% secure.</p><hr/><h1><strong>7. Data Retention</strong></h1><p>We retain personal data only for as long as necessary to fulfill:</p><ul><li>Business purposes</li><li>Customer support</li><li>Contract obligations</li><li>Legal and regulatory requirements</li></ul><p>Afterward, we delete or anonymize the data securely.</p><hr/><h1><strong>8. Your Rights</strong></h1><p>Depending on your jurisdiction (GDPR, CCPA, etc.), you may have the right to:</p><ul><li>Access your personal information</li><li>Correct or update your data</li><li>Request deletion (“right to be forgotten”)</li><li>Restrict or object to processing</li><li>Withdraw consent</li><li>Data portability</li><li>Opt out of marketing communications</li></ul><p>To exercise these rights:<br/>📧 <strong><a class="decorated-link cursor-pointer" rel="noopener"><span class="__cf_email__">[email protected]</span></a></strong></p><hr/><h1><strong>9. Children’s Privacy</strong></h1><p>Our website and services are <strong>not intended for individuals under 13 years old</strong>.<br/>We do not knowingly collect personal information from children.</p><hr/><h1><strong>10. International Data Transfers</strong></h1><p>Since we serve global customers, your information may be processed outside your country.<br/>We ensure appropriate safeguards are applied, such as:</p><ul><li>Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs)</li><li>Secure international hosting environments</li><li>Compliance with international data-transfer regulations</li></ul><hr/><h1><strong>11. Changes to This Policy</strong></h1><p>We may update this Privacy Policy when necessary for legal, technical, or business reasons.<br/>Changes will be posted on this page with the updated <strong>Effective Date</strong>. For major changes, we may also notify you via email or website alerts.</p><hr/><h1><strong>12. Contact Us</strong></h1><p>If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or your data rights, please contact:</p><p><strong>Email:</strong> <a class="decorated-link cursor-pointer" rel="noopener"><span class="__cf_email__">[email protected]</span></a><br/><strong>Website:</strong> <a class="decorated-link" href="" rel="noopener" target="_new"></a></p></div>`} />
